# Clean-arch boundaries (features)

Applies to feature work under `sprout_app/lib/features/**`. Details: `.cursor/references/architecture.md`.

## Barrel exports

- Feature barrel files must be named `export.dart`.
- Import from `package:sprout/features/<feature>/export.dart` (not `.../<feature>.dart`).

## UI-only pages

- Files under `sprout_app/lib/features/**/presentation/**_page.dart` (and `*_screen.dart`) must be UI-only.
- Do not define `enum`s, top-level helper functions, or sorting/business logic in pages.
- Extract non-UI code to `presentation/utils/**` or a bloc/service.

## Reusable UI

- If the same UI pattern appears in 2+ features, extract a shared widget under `sprout_app/lib/ui/**`.
- Feature UI may depend on `lib/ui/**`. Shared UI must not import feature code.
- Shared UI stays dumb: inputs + callbacks; no `sl<>`, repositories, or feature services.
- Keep async work (save/delete/fetch) in the feature bloc/service; pass a callback/result into the widget.

## Enums location

- UI-specific enums: `presentation/enums/**`.
- Domain-wide enums: `domain/enums/**` (or next to the entity if there is a single enum).

## Models and mapping

- Frontend entities: `domain/**`.
- Hive/Supabase DTOs: `data/local/models/**` and `data/remote/models/**`.
- Mapping: `data/mappers/**` (or a feature `data/*_mapper.dart` barrel).

## Dependency direction

- `presentation/**` may depend on `domain/**` and `application/**`.
- `presentation/**` must not import `data/local/**`, `data/remote/**`, or `data/**/models/**`.
